WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:10.040
The fictional campaign brief keeps approved facts separate from the requester’s draft.

2
00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:18.880
Open the partner-promotion brief to see its draft and approved facts.

3
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:29.760
The draft includes figures and claims for the brand check to review.

4
00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:37.400
Approved facts give the writer the claims and figures to use.

5
00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:55.080
Submitting the brief starts writing, brand checks and revision.

6
00:00:55.080 --> 00:01:03.100
The revised copy is ready for the marketing decision.

7
00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:11.600
Open the held brief to review the checked version.

8
00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:23.120
Each brand-rule finding gives the writer a specific correction.

9
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:36.840
Rewritten channel copy keeps approved facts and removes unsupported claims.

10
00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:44.920
The revised copy passes the configured brand checks.

11
00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:53.800
The brief lists omitted requests alongside the copy for marketing.

12
00:01:53.840 --> 00:02:02.620
The exact copy version waits for its marketing decision.

13
00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:13.900
The workflow writes, checks and revises before holding the copy for marketing.

14
00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:29.980
The decisions board brings the campaign review records together.

15
00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:35.820
Typed by Claude (automated test) as the marketing approver.

16
00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:46.260
The decision names the held brief and records the automated approver’s note.

17
00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:50.260
Saving the decision starts the approval workflow.

18
00:02:50.300 --> 00:03:03.700
The workflow checks the decision against the held record before resuming.

19
00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:15.180
The recorded decision applies once to the waiting copy.

20
00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:21.620
The checked brief now carries its recorded approval.

21
00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:30.260
Open the approved brief to see the decision with its copy.

22
00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:39.740
The resumed workflow records the automated approver, copy version and decision time.

23
00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:49.340
The approved version is ready for the publishing team’s handoff.
